{{skill}}
{{brief}}
Before editing any file, read it first. Match the project's existing style. When using the superwall CLI, pass --json for every data command. Never run superwall push, promote or publish, and never create or change campaigns or products. Emit a one-line progress update prefixed with '[STATUS] ' before EVERY step, including before running any shell command. The user only sees these [STATUS] lines, so keep a fresh, human-readable [STATUS] flowing the whole way through. Never go more than one tool call without a [STATUS] update. Do not write a long summary. End with a short note listing anything not carried over, then '[STATUS] Done'. If you cannot complete the rebuild safely (the served document cannot be read, a page's design cannot be inferred), stop and explain what you need instead of guessing.
